<title>AUSTRALIA: State Opposition says S.Australia plans to sell power co.</title>
<headline>State Opposition says S.Australia plans to sell power co.</headline>
<dateline>ADELAIDE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South Australian Labor Opposition said on Tuesday the state government was planning to sell off the Electricity Trust of SA (ETSA) if it won control of both houses of parliament at the next election.</p>
<p>The Liberal government has denied any such plans and rejected Opposition claims that overseas energy firms had visited Adelaide as recently as last week to inspect ETSA in the leadup to privatisation.</p>
</text>
